#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:2
msgid "Making a pull request (PR) — how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:4
msgid ""
"Pull requests are used to contribute code and documentation changes to ROS "
"projects. This article explains how to prepare and create a pull request "
"from your fork of a ROS repository. With this information, you'll be able to "
"submit focused changes in a pull request, ready for review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:8
msgid ""
"**Area: contributing, community | Content-type: how-to | Experience: "
"beginner, intermediate, expert**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:12
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:15
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:17
msgid ""
"`Pull requests (PRs) <https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests>`__ are "
"proposals to merge your changes into a ROS repository. Making a pull request "
"allows you to collaborate with other ROS contributors, providing a space to "
"discuss and review your code changes before a ROS maintainer merges them. "
"Pull requests are welcome for any of `the ROS repositories <https://github."
"com/ros2>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:21
msgid ""
"For more information about contribution etiquette, see :doc:`Contributing </"
"The-ROS2-Project/Contributing>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:24
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:26
msgid ""
"`Create a fork <https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-"
"pull-requests/working-with-forks/fork-a-repo>`__ of the target ROS "
"repository for your code changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:27
msgid ""
"Complete your code changes on a development branch taken from the "
"**rolling** branch, in your fork of the `target ROS repository <https://"
"github.com/ros2>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:28
msgid "Make sure your changes comply with ROS guidelines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:30
msgid "If your pull request is for a code change:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:32
msgid ""
"Make sure you've followed the guidance in the :doc:`Developer guide </The-"
"ROS2-Project/Contributing/Developer-Guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:33
msgid ""
"Check that your code complies with the relevant section of the :doc:`Code "
"style guide </The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Code-Style-Language-Versions>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:34
msgid ""
"Make sure you've :ref:`run the tests <colcon-run-the-tests>` and the "
"appropriate linter for your code changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:36
msgid "If your pull request is for a documentation change:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:38
msgid ""
"Make sure you've followed the guidance in :doc:`/The-ROS2-Project/"
"Contributing/Contributing-To-ROS-2-Documentation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:41
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:44
msgid "1 Preparing the pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:46
msgid "Use the following guidelines to prepare your pull request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:48
msgid "**Scope and focus**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:49
msgid "Limit each pull request to a single, well-defined change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:50
msgid "Submit unrelated changes as separate pull requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:51
msgid "Keep patches small and avoid unnecessary or incidental changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:52
msgid "**Commit history and squashing**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:53
msgid ""
"Squash changes into a minimum number of clear, semantic commits to preserve "
"a readable project history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:54
msgid ""
"Don't squash commits while a pull request is under review, as reviewers may "
"not notice changes which can lead to confusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:55
msgid "You can create new commits while a pull request is under review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:56
msgid "**Draft pull requests**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:57
msgid ""
"Use draft pull requests to request early feedback while work is in progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:58
msgid ""
"Don't expect draft pull requests to be formally reviewed or merged until you "
"have marked them as ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:59
msgid ""
"If you want early feedback from a specific person on a draft pull request, "
"mention them (using ``@``) in the pull request description or in a comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:60
msgid "**Mentions and references**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:61
msgid ""
"If your changes are based on a design document, such as a `REP <https://reps."
"openrobotics.org/>`__, mention other people involved in the design, such as "
"those who reviewed the REP, in the pull request description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:62
msgid ""
"If your pull request depends on another pull request, clearly reference the "
"dependency in the pull request description. Ensure to mention the pull "
"request ID using ``#`` notation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:64
msgid ""
"If your changes are planned to be released with a specific version of ROS, "
"include that version of ROS in the pull request description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:65
msgid "**Documenting your code changes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:66
msgid ""
"If your pull request is for code changes, try to make any relevant "
"documentation updates (including API documentation, feature documentation, "
"and release notes) in the same pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:69
msgid "2 Submitting the pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:71
msgid ""
"Create a pull request from the branch containing your changes in your fork, "
"to the **rolling** branch of the target ROS repository. You can create your "
"pull request using the GitHub CLI, GitHub Desktop, or the GitHub web "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:74
msgid ""
"For more information about creating a pull request from a fork, see `the "
"GitHub documentation <https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-"
"with-pull-requests/proposing-changes-to-your-work-with-pull-requests/"
"creating-a-pull-request-from-a-fork>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:76
msgid ""
"For more information about each of the available pull request methods, see "
"`the GitHub documentation <https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/"
"collaborating-with-pull-requests/proposing-changes-to-your-work-with-pull-"
"requests/creating-a-pull-request>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:78
msgid ""
"Populate the pull request by completing the sections shown in the "
"description template, including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:80
msgid ""
"**Description**: summarize your code changes, linking to related GitHub "
"issue(s) and PRs by ID, highlighting any key points or areas of concern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:81
msgid ""
"**Issue**: include the ID of the GitHub issue fixed by your changes, in the "
"format ``Fixes #(issue)``. This ensures that the issue is automatically "
"closed when the pull request is merged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:83
msgid ""
"**Generative AI**: if this pull request was generated using Generative AI, "
"specify the model and version (for example, GitHub Copilot v3.2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:84
msgid ""
"**Additional information**: provide any context or details you think will be "
"useful for understanding your changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:86
msgid ""
"Select the `Allow edits by maintainers <https://github.blog/news-insights/"
"product-news/improving-collaboration-with-forks/>`__ checkbox, to help ROS "
"maintainers make small changes directly when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:88
msgid ""
"After you've submitted your pull request, other developers and contributors "
"in the ROS community will review your changes, including checking against "
"the relevant guidelines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:91
msgid "3 Responding to review comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:93
msgid ""
"When another developer or contributor adds a review comment or suggestion to "
"your pull request, you will receive a notification from GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:95
msgid ""
"You can view and discuss review comments directly in GitHub (see `the GitHub "
"documentation for assistance <https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/"
"collaborating-with-pull-requests/reviewing-changes-in-pull-requests/viewing-"
"a-pull-request-review>`__), and add further commits to your branch to "
"address them when needed. You can also directly accept any suggested changes "
"in the pull request, which adds a new commit to your branch automatically "
"(see `the GitHub documentation for how to accept suggested changes <https://"
"docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-pull-requests/reviewing-"
"changes-in-pull-requests/incorporating-feedback-in-your-pull-request>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:98
msgid ""
"Discuss and iterate on your changes with this feedback, amending and "
"updating your development branch with new commits as needed. Aim to reply "
"back to review comments within one week, so that you and the reviewers do "
"not lose the context of your changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:102
msgid "4 Merging the pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:104
msgid ""
"After you've actioned any feedback, your pull request must be approved by a :"
"doc:`Committer for the target ROS repository </The-ROS2-Project/Governance>` "
"before it can be merged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:106
msgid ""
"When the Committer approves your pull request, they will merge it to the "
"target branch (usually **rolling**), and you will receive a notification "
"from GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR.rst:108
msgid "Your changes may also be backported to older distributions of ROS."
msgstr ""

